  "worked_solution": "To graph the first inequality $y>x+2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=x+2.$\n\n- Since we have a strict inequality, the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y<2x-2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2x-2.$\n\n- Since we have a strict inequality, the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/9d367b12f56fde031940dc3194f8300eb4d5e40b9ec793c7d35a5808f5d14996.png)",
